<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chittagong</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Chattogram</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Chittagong, officially Chattogram, is the main port and second-largest city of Bangladesh, on the Karnaphuli river near the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bay-of-bengal">Bay of Bengal</a>. A trading port since ancient times, it was contested by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bengal">Bengal</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tripura">Tripura</a> and Arakan, held by the Arakanese kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mrauk-u">Mrauk U</a> in the 16th and 17th centuries, and taken by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mughal-empire">Mughals</a> in 1666. It passed to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-india-company">East India Company</a> in 1760.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/chittagong.jpg" alt="Chittagong" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Great Hero32 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jamburi_park,_Agrabad,_Chittagong_2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
